Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:16:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Post the venue the contract answers 404 for
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The unknown-venue test posted "Nowhere, Atlantis", the contract's
existing 200 [] example, so it passed with or without the 404 branch:
the mutants on geocoder_client.py's new lines survived. It now posts
"Unknown Venue, Nowhere", the example this change adds, whose 404 body is
a trap a client that reads it would turn into coordinates.

Hand-written L0 fixture for ticket 0013's attempt 2 (docs/adr/0038 §10):
the answer to attempt 1's mutation verdict. No model wrote it.
---
 app/backend/tests/test_meetups.py | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/backend/tests/test_meetups.py b/app/backend/tests/test_meetups.py
index 951fd36..1afffb9 100644
--- a/app/backend/tests/test_meetups.py
+++ b/app/backend/tests/test_meetups.py
@@ -51,15 +51,15 @@ def test_get_unknown_meetup_is_404(client):
 
 
 def test_unknown_venue_returns_201_with_null_coordinates(client, geocoder_server):
-    # Ticket 0013: an unknown venue means the meetup is still created, with
-    # null coordinates.
+    # Ticket 0013: the geocoder 404s on a venue it doesn't know. That is
+    # "no result", not "dependency broken" -- the meetup is still created.
     token = _signup_and_login(client, "unknown-venue@example.com")
     create = client.post(
         "/api/meetups",
         json={
             "title": "Somewhere else",
             "starts_at": "2026-03-01T18:00:00Z",
-            "venue": "Nowhere, Atlantis",
+            "venue": "Unknown Venue, Nowhere",
             "capacity": 5,
         },
         headers=_auth(token),
